    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c68f0d1a_00d68acb",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/CommandBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-19T13:09:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think for now this is an okay struct. We\u0027ll obviously need a way to describe subpasses, multiple color attachments, etc.\n\nFor the resolve we\u0027ll have to figure out what the best api is. Vulkan treats the resolve as an attachment. Metal and Dawn assign a resolve texture to each color attachment. D3D12 render passes (which we aren\u0027t using yet) don\u0027t even look like they have a resolve option on them. My guess is an API like this where the resolve isn\u0027t passed as an attachment will work. But then for Vulkan that will be a lot of behind the scenes stuff promoting it to an attachment and setting up an input attachment on the subpass.\n\nUntil we get more of sense of how things will fit together its not clear to me whether to make the higher level handle setting all the up or hid those details internally here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 25,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "4850a7764ec5ee309348e375aefd681bf3d30d14",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
